\mainpage ⚓️ The Lost Age

\htmlonly<p class="game-banner game-tla"><span class="mark">&#x2693;&#xFE0F;</span>Golden Sun: The Lost Age, still being matched. Code inside <code>#if</code> follows the English edition (<code>TLA_EDITION_EN</code>); what only another edition builds is in the source files but not on these pages.</p>\endhtmlonly

About a third of The Lost Age's code is C so far, and nearly all of its data
is placed from source; the README's progress chart has the current figures.
These pages show that C, in \c games/tla. The rest still comes from the
cartridge through the scaffold in \c recon/tla, with drafts of the functions
being matched; neither is shown here.

Most of its C has not been read for meaning yet. A function or global named
by its address, such as \c Func_02001140, is a placeholder until evidence
gives it a name, and so is a field named by its offset. Each folder's guide says what differs from The Broken Seal's, whose guides
describe the same engine; most of its names carry over.

Its folders, each with its guide (the maps are tables and assembly, with no C):

